> That sounds like a bug, right?

Well, I think yes but I did not know if it was done in purpose ...
Here is the quick changes I did, but there might be a better solution.
``` 
bool MavsdkImpl::send_message(mavlink_message_t& message)
{
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(_connections_mutex);

    uint succesfull_emissions = 0;
    for (auto it = _connections.begin(); it != _connections.end(); ++it) {
        if ((**it).send_message(message)) {
            succesfull_emissions++;
        }
    }

    if (succesfull_emissions == 0) {
        LogErr() << "send fail";
        return false;
    }

    return true;
}
```


> Yes, I think that would be a good optimization.

All right, I thought of adding a std:vector<uint8_t> in Connection class protected attributes, and a method to check for system ID existence.
I will add it to the corresponding branch, and initialize a pull request.

